<title>TAIWAN: TAIWAN BSPA BUYS 112,000T OF US SOYBEANS AT TENDER.</title>
<headline>TAIWAN BSPA BUYS 112,000T OF US SOYBEANS AT TENDER.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Taichung division of Taiwan's Breakfast Soybean Procurement Association bought two 56,000-tonne shipments of U.S. soybeans from Continental and Bunge at a tender on Wednesday, traders said.  </p>
<p>The Breakfast association's Taichung division comprises Sino Japan Feed Corp, Chia Hsin, Formosa Oilseed, Fwu Sow Grain, and Tay Shan.</p>
<p>Details for the tender are as follows:</p>
<p> Tonnes  Date/Location		    Prices/Futures</p>
<p>	   U.S. Gulf	Pacific N.W.</p>
<p> 56,000  Oct  7-21	Oct 22-Nov 7  110.89 US Cents/Nov</p>
<p>-- or --</p>
<p>	   U.S. Gulf	Pacific N.W.</p>
<p> 56,000  Oct 28-Nov 11  Nov 12-27     105.28 US Cents/Nov</p>
